      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "consequence",
      "statement": "The after-source depth helper reports \"Exceeded maximum allowed query depth\" through error(), which stores the error and lexer offset in the parse result and returns null.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-0f1db7bf65d8d03af75c", "start_line": 11184, "end_line": 11187, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-ceec7f3ebb73bf24bdac", "start_line": 11168, "end_line": 11174, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "Shows how the depth error is recorded."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "The supplied before-source public constructor calls xpath_parser::parse and throws xpath_exception for a parse failure when exceptions are enabled. This establishes the public-to-parser route before the change, but the corresponding after-source constructor definition was not supplied.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-1e3b5ce7e1524353bd71", "start_line": 12604, "end_line": 12640, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-7e5aa7af393e89a4abcb", "start_line": 12084, "end_line": 12089, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "Shows the after-source parser's static entry point, without establishing that the public constructor calls it."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "counterevidence",
      "statement": "In the exception-enabled harness branch, xpath_exception from query construction is caught. In the no-exceptions branch, construction is invoked without inspecting its result.",
